   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "rgbrenner",
     "replies": 20,
     "text": "Forget about the scores... look at the Cost Per Task. Fable 5.1 was already the most expensive by a good margin, and now Fable 5.2 doubles it! This is with the price cut.\nThe output tokens per task just exploded. From 118k tokens (46k Answer/71k Reasoning) in 5.1 to 274k tokens (81k Answer/192k Reasoning) in 5.2."
    },
    {
     "author": "oliwary",
     "replies": 5,
     "text": "Cool! It looks like Fable 5.2 (especially low and medium) also sit on the pareto frontier between time per task and intelligence: https://artificialanalysis.ai/models?speed=output-speed-over...\nI am always interested in this comparison since it shows how quickly you can go back and forth with a model, capturing both tokens/task and tokens/second. The new models seem to be meaningfully better here."
    },
    {
     "author": "brachkow",
     "replies": 8,
     "text": "It's crazy how expensive Anthropic's model is compared to pretty capable DeepSeek-Flash\nWhile they made, hands down, the best models, their 100x price for few percent better is completely made up, and I think it will end up bad for them"
    },
    {
     "author": "schnitzelstoat",
     "replies": 2,
     "text": "That seems like an insane increase in cost for a modest intelligence increase.\nBut perhaps the performance on real-world tasks will be more noticeable than on benchmarks."
    },
    {
     "author": "rodorgas",
     "replies": 2,
     "text": "Artificial Analysis is paid by AI labs and they don't publish the full method. To me it's meaningless, let's wait for other benchmarks, but if they're correct the intelligence increment is negligible."
    }
   ],
   "article": {
    "url": "https://artificialanalysis.ai/models/claude-fable-5-2",
    "status": "ok",
    "title": "Claude Fable 5.2 (max) - Intelligence, Performance & Price Analysis | Artificial Analysis",
    "chars": 15259,
    "text": "Artificial Analysis\nAnthropic\n•\nClaude Fable 5.2\n•\nProprietary model\n•\nReleased November 2026\nClaude Fable 5.2 (Max, Default Fallback) Intelligence, Performance & Price Analysis\nTry it out API Provider Benchmarks\nModel summary\nIntelligenceUpdated\n65\nArtificial Analysis Intelligence Index\n4 out of 4 units for Intelligence.\nPerformance\nTime to first answer token 230.35sOutput speed 103 tok/s\n44.4\nTime per Intelligence Index task (minutes)\n4 out of 4 units for Performance.\nCost\nIn $8.00Out $40.00Cache discount 98%\n$26.54\nCost per Intelligence Index task\n4 out of 4 units for Cost.\nVerbosity\nInput tokens 28.3BOutput/input 0.97%\n275M\nOutput tokens from Intelligence Index\n4 out of 4 units for Verbosity.\nClaude Fable 5.2 (Max, Default Fallback) is amongst the leading models in intelligence, but particularly expensive when comparing to other models of similar price. It's also notably slow per task and very verbose. The model supports text and image input, outputs text, and has a 1M tokens context window.\nClaude Fable 5.2 (Max, Default Fallback) scores 65 on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index, placing it well above average among comparable models (median: 40). When evaluating the Intelligence Index, it generated 275M tokens, which is very verbose in comparison to the median of 72.8M.\nPricing for Claude Fable 5.2 (Max, Default Fallback) is $8.00 per 1M input tokens (expensive, median: $2.00) and $40.00 per 1M output tokens (expensive, median: $10.00). On average, it costs $26.54 per task to evaluate Claude Fable 5.2 (Max, Default Fallback) on the Intelligence Index.\nAt 44.4 minutes per Intelligence Index task, Claude Fable 5.2 (Max, Default Fallback) is notably slow compared with the median of 12.8 minutes for comparable models (lower is better).\nReasoningYes\nThis page shows the reasoning version of this model.\nA non-reasoning variant may also exist.\nInput modality\nSupports: text and image\nOutput modality\nSupports: text\nContext window1M\n~1500 A4 pages of size 12 Arial font\nMetrics are compared against models of the same class:\nNon-reasoning models → compared only with other non-reasoning models\nReasoning models → compared across both reasoning and non-reasoning\nOpen weights models → compared only with other open weights models of the same size class:\nTiny: ≤4B parameters\nSmall: 4B–40B parameters\nMedium: 40B–150B parameters\nLarge: >150B parameters\nProprietary models → compared across proprietary and open weights models of the same price range, using a blended 3:1 input/output price ratio:\n<$0.15 per 1M tokens\n$0.15–$1 per 1M tokens\n>$1 per 1M tokens\nUpdated\nIntelligence\nArtificial Analysis Intelligence Index · Higher is better\nNo publicly available API\nTime per Task\nInference time (minutes) per Intelligence Index task · Lower is better\nNo publicly available API\nCost per Task\nWeighted average cost (USD) per Intelligence Index task · Lower is better\nNo publicly available API\nIntelligenceUpdated\nArtificial Analysis Intelligence Index\nArtificial Analysis Intelligence Index v5.0.1 incorporates 9 evaluations: AA-Briefcase v1.1, AutomationBench-AA, Terminal-Bench 4.0, FrontierCode 2.0, AA-Omniscience v1.1, GDP.pdf, HLE-Diamond, CritPt v2 (Hard Subset), and Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1\nNo publicly available API\nArtificial Analysis Intelligence Index v5.0.1 includes: AA-Briefcase v1.1, AutomationBench-AA, Terminal-Bench 4.0, FrontierCode 2.0, AA-Omniscience v1.1, GDP.pdf, HLE-Diamond, CritPt v2 (Hard Subset), Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1. See Intelligence Index methodology for further details, including a breakdown of each evaluation and how we run them.\nArtificial Analysis Intelligence Index by Open Weights / Proprietary\nArtificial Analysis Intelligence Index v5.0.1 incorporates 9 evaluations: AA-Briefcase v1.1, AutomationBench-AA, Terminal-Bench 4.0, FrontierCode 2.0, AA-Omniscience v1.1, GDP.pdf, HLE-Diamond, CritPt v2 (Hard Subset), and Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1\nNo publicly available API\nArtificial Analysis Intelligence Index v5.0.1…"
